    <dataSetInformation>
      <common:UUID>552f63d9-e491-4d92-9c16-138e43d6ae3d</common:UUID>
      <name>
        <baseName xml:lang="en">Concrete C12/15_X0_S4_F, at production, IT</baseName>
      </name>
      <common:synonyms>C12/15_X0_S4_F, alla produzione, IT</common:synonyms>
      <classificationInformation>
        <common:classification name="ILCDCategories" classes="../ILCDClassification.xml">
          <common:class level="0">Systems</common:class>
          <common:class level="1">Construction</common:class>
        </common:classification>
      </classificationInformation>
      <common:generalComment>Dataset developed according to Arcadia project Methodology (Report: “Metodologia per gli studi di filiera della Banca Dati italiana LCA”). LCA study of concrete production (Report: “Studio LCA della filiera del calcestruzzo”). This dataset is representative of the average ready mix concretes with strength class C12/15, exposure class X0, slump class S4 and 100% crushed aggregates defined by the UNI EN 206 produced in Italy.</common:generalComment>
      <referenceToExternalDocumentation type="source data set" refObjectId="36f625af-7d9d-404a-b4f2-89d17a1644af" version="01.00.000" uri="../sources/36f625af-7d9d-404a-b4f2-89d17a1644af.xml">
        <common:shortDescription>Background datasets from Ecoinvent database cut-off (v.3.8) were used for the LCA study.</common:shortDescription>
      </referenceToExternalDocumentation>
    </dataSetInformation>
    <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
      <referenceToReferenceFlow>0</referenceToReferenceFlow>
    </quantitativeReference>
    <time>
      <common:referenceYear>2021</common:referenceYear>
      <common:dataSetValidUntil>2026</common:dataSetValidUntil>
    </time>
    <geography>
      <locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction location="IT"/>
    </geography>
    <technology>
      <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>The ready mix concrete production process includes the clinker, cement, aggregates, additives production stages. Clinker is produced from natural raw materials (such as limestone, clay, gypsum, marl and others) which are crushed, finely ground, homogenised and fired in a blast furnace. Once out, the clinker is cooled and ground in the mills with the addition of other natural raw materials (mainly gypsum and limestone) and other materials/additives to obtain the final homogeneous powder (the cement). &#13;
Cement is subsequently mixed with aggregates, water and additives in concrete mixing plant.&#13;
For the background processes (raw material in input) EcoInvent database (v. 3.8) cut-off datasets were used. &#13;
Reliability 'Very good';&#13;
Geographical representation 'Very good';&#13;
Temporal representativeness 'Very good’;&#13;
Technological representativeness ‘Very good’&#13;
</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
      <technologicalApplicability>Production of italian ready mix concrete for construction sector</technologicalApplicability>
    </technology>
  </processInformation>
